  "thumbnailAlt": "Pet Adoption Application form beside a photo of dogs waiting behind a fence at an animal shelter",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A pet adoption application is a form that collects an adopter's household, home type, landlord permission, current and past pets, vet reference and daily routine so a shelter or rescue can match the right animal to the right home. This template asks the questions that predict a lasting adoption, such as hours alone, yard and fencing, and plans if circumstances change, and lets applicants upload a home photo or lease clause.",
    "audience": "Animal shelters, foster-based rescues, breed rescues, humane societies, cat cafés and responsible breeders rehoming retired animals.",
    "useCases": [
      "An Adopt Me button on every animal profile on your website",
      "Adoption events where visitors apply on their phone by QR code",
      "Breed rescues screening applicants across several states",
      "Foster-to-adopt programs where fosters apply to keep their pet"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Use conditional logic to ask for landlord permission only when the applicant rents.",
      "Turn on edit history so your team can see who updated an application after the home check.",
      "Add the email copy to the respondent so applicants have a record and know what happens next."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a pet adoption application include?",
        "answer": "Contact details and age confirmation, the animal they are applying for, household members and children's ages, home type, whether they own or rent and have landlord permission, yard and fencing, current and past pets with vaccination status, a vet reference, hours the pet will be alone, exercise and care plans, what they would do if they could no longer keep the pet, and consent to a home check."
      },
      {
        "question": "Why do rescues ask for landlord permission?",
        "answer": "Housing that does not allow pets is a common reason animals are returned to shelters. Confirming permission before adoption protects the animal and the adopter."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do shelters contact my vet?",
        "answer": "Many do, to confirm that current pets are vaccinated, neutered and seen regularly. The application asks for permission before anyone calls."
      },
      {
        "question": "How long does pet adoption approval take?",
        "answer": "It varies by organization, from same-day approvals at some shelters to one or two weeks at foster-based rescues that do reference and home checks."
      }
    ]
  },
